title:VeraF1W
---
Vera: The stars are so bright today, I can’t take my eyes off them.
Loveday: (Are stars not visible where she’s originally from?)
	-> Do you like the stars?
	    Vera: Yes, I love the stars!
	    Vera: It’s only until recently I’ve learned the wonders that lie in the sky. 
        Loveday: I assume you’re not accustomed to seeing them this bright? You are from (insert main city here.) I heard the lights make it harder to see the stars.
        Vera: Wow, you’re correct!
        Vera: My days used to be filled with fog that was within arms-reach.

    -> Leave her to gaze.
===

title:ElsieF2W
---
Elsie: To think Vera had to go through such monstrosities… Vampires really are wicked.
Loveday: Truly.
Elsie: She’s always so happy… I wonder why she never told us… <i>*hic hic hic*</i> P-Poor Vera…!
Loveday: Don’t worry. She has us. She has other people to live for now.
Elsie: Hehe… You’re right… Speaking of other people, Dahlia fed me today…
Loveday: Is that not a daily occurrence? Why act as if it is rare?
Elsie: N-no! It’s different!
Elsie: I’ve always studied how humans treat food as a sacred, intimate thing, so to experience that with her… you wouldn’t understand! 
Loveday: (I really don’t.)
===




title:VeraF2W
---
Vera: Ahoy hoy, Loveday!!
Vera: I have a question for you! A lifetime supply of hardtack for the rest of your life, or a gill of rum a week? 
    -> Obviously the rum. 
        Vera: Oooh yeah. Rum’s a good choice!
        Vera: If we had any, you’d probably be drinking your sorrows away!
        Loveday: What’s that supposed to mean?!

    -> Why would I pick the hardtack? 
        Vera: Oh. What do you mean? 
        Loveday: It’s… disgusting. 
        Vera: Oh… I think it tastes great. 
        Loveday: <i>(So that’s where all of it’s been going…)</i>

===

title:DahliaF2W
---
Dahlia: Yo, captain. 
Loveday: Hey.
Dahlia: I can’t wait to go back home and tell Santhe about my adventures. 
Dahlia: Who knows? Maybe with Vera’s cooking advice, he might actually stomach the food I make.
Loveday: (Something tells me deep down Santhe is just as stubborn as his sister.)
	-> Most likely not.
        Dahlia: Seriously? Is it that bad?
        Loveday: Yes. Even Vera, who thrives on a diet of hardtacks, criticizes your lack of cooking skills. 
	-> Perhaps. 
        Dahlia: Huh? Goin’ soft on me now?
        Loveday: I take it back.
	    Dahlia: Ugh! Whatever.
        Dahlia: I heard too much seasoning makes vampire blood sour anyways. You know who I have to keep myself sweet for.
	    Loveday: That’s disgusting. 

===

